# 0088-discard-the-partial-build.patch -- the owner's point P: "a game whose build was PAUSED part-way cannot be deleted". Applies after 0087. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR:
# compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# P. "Discard the partial build" (red, trash icon), wherever the paused game shows: its touch-and-hold menu (right after "Cancel the paused build…"), the Build tab's card under Resume and
#    Cancel (its words do not fit a third of the card), and the iPad's hero beside Resume (a paused game has no inspector: only a built game has settings, 0082). It works on the game it is
#    shown for, whichever game is selected (the card's paused game: CardPaused).
#    - The rule (GameAppField.cs PartialDiscard.For): offered for a paused build; REFUSED, greyed with its reason under the title (and as the VoiceOver hint; a tap in the menu shows it), while
#      that build runs or pauses ("It is building: pause it first, then discard it."), while another build or a game runs (extract/ may be that one's), and when the game file is a stub
#      (Optimize storage: the extraction is all that is left to build it from). Built, not built, cloud and downloading games: not offered.
#    - The question (sizes measured off the main thread, FolderWalk): "Discard the partial build of <game>?" / "Removes the extracted game (13.0 GB), the rewrite and the 1,234 shaders
#      translated so far; the game file itself stays." (the count from the paused build's stage line; none before the shader step; "the extracted game is another build's now: it stays"
#      when a later build replaced it) + "Every finished shader stays in the shader cache (a new build reuses it); the game's settings, saves, cover and mods are not touched. The game is
#      "Not built" again." Buttons "Discard (13.4 GB)" (destructive) / "Keep it".
#    - The discard (asked again at the confirmation: a Resume may have started): 0065's cancel cleanup with PartialDiscard.Plan: extract/ (when it is this game's: the paused record and the
#      slot say so), shaders/<id>.work with its pause marker, the partial DmGameProbe.framework and gameapp.framework, AND the extraction marker gameapp.extracted and profile.tsv (a cancel
#      kept them); the folders on the delete worker, never the main thread; the paused record goes (gameapp.paused.tsv), the queue entry too; never shadercache/, games/<id>/ or the game
#      file, its update or DLC (CancelPlan.Forbidden, checked). Then the free space is read again (DiskFreeNow), the sizes and the slot refreshed, the game is "Not built", and the log says
#      "partial build discarded: <title>, 13.4 GB freed".
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile (-t:Compile):
#   0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness88: … P87;P88): 288 of 288 checks (18 new: which states offer it, refuse it or not, the menu,
#   the question's words, the shader count, the plan and what it never touches, the log line, the wiring); 13 of 13 mutations killed.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: the real sizes and the free space after a discard, the greyed rows' look, a discard of a game other than the selected one.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Discard the partial build", "Discard the partial build of ", "the extracted game (", " translated so far", "; the game file itself stays.", "Discard (", "Discard",
#   "Keep it", the three reasons (PartialDiscard.RunningWhy, OtherWhy, StubWhy), PartialDiscard.Keeps, "The build is no longer paused."; log lines "partial build discarded: ",
#   "partial build: discarding ", "partial build: not discarded: ".
